  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This was reported as fixed in 2024.4.1p3 but it looks like the problem crept back in and exists in SDK 3.8.2 / 2025.3.1 (haven't tested any other versions).  Since the previous canny was closed out as complete, thought I'd open a new one.\n\nPrior bug report on this issue:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/udon/p/braces-inside-strings-in-vrcjson-can-fail-to-deserialize\n\n// This works\n\nif(VRCJson.TryDeserializeFromJson(\"\\\"{\\\"data\\\":\\\"test\\\"}\", out DataToken token2))\n\n    Debug.LogError(\"Failed to deserialize JSON\");\n\nelse\n\n    Debug.Log(\"Successfully deserialized JSON\");\n\n// This fails.  Only difference is the braces after the word test in the JSON string.  Number of braces or their configuration doesn't seem to make a difference.\n\nif(VRCJson.TryDeserializeFromJson(\"{\\\"data\\\":\\\"test{}\\\"}\", out DataToken token1))\n\n    Debug.LogError(\"Failed to deserialize JSON\");\n\nelse\n\n    Debug.Log(\"Successfully deserialized JSON\");\n\nThanks!  -Tea",
